@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Build menu hitches
+
+## Problem
+
+Each page was rebuilt from nothing every time it was shown:
+
+- `BuildMenu.luau` used `switch(props.Tab)`, so changing tabs destroyed the old page and
+  created the new one. That's about 450 instances for Shapes (a 40 ms frame) and about 370 for
+  Colors (30 ms). Colors also creates 120 reactive stroke effects.
+- `Main.client.luau` wrapped the whole menu in `show(isMenuOpen, ...)`, so closing destroyed the
+  menu after its slide-out and opening rebuilt it, including whichever page was current.
+
+## Change
+
+- **The menu is mounted once** (`Main.client.luau`). `Present` is now `isMenuOpen` directly.
+  The panel still slides in and out using the same spring, and its `Visible` goes false only
+  when the slide-out has finished (`panelShown` in `BuildMenu.luau`).
+- **Pages are kept** (`keptPage` in `BuildMenu.luau`). A page is built the first time its tab is
+  shown in an open menu. After that it stays alive, and switching tabs only sets `Visible`.
+  Nothing is built at startup, so a page you never open costs nothing.
+- **The rainbow swatch only updates while you can see it.** Its Heartbeat handler skips frames
+  when the Colors page or the panel is hidden, so the kept page costs nothing while hidden.
+
+Layout, colors, sizes and the slide animation are unchanged. One small difference: the rainbow
+swatch used to restart at red every time Colors opened. Now it continues from the hue it was on.
+
+The first visit to Shapes or Colors still costs the same as before, because each page is built
+once. If that matters too, the pages could be built ahead of time over a few frames.
+
+## Checking it in Studio
+
+1. Play Solo, then open the MicroProfiler (Ctrl+F6). Pause it with Ctrl+P when you want to
+   look at a frame.
+2. Open the menu (M) and visit Shapes and Colors once each. These first visits will still
+   spike, which is expected.
+3. Switch between Blocks, Colors and Shapes several times, and close and reopen the menu with
+   M while it's on Shapes or Colors. Those frames should now stay near your usual ~8 ms, with
+   no 30–40 ms spikes.
+4. To count instances, open the Explorer under
+   `Players > <you> > PlayerGui > BuildMenuGui > BuildMenu > Page` while playing. After the
+   first visits there's one child per page you've opened (`Blocks`, `Colors`, `Shapes`).
+   Switching tabs only flips their `Visible` property. No children are added or removed, and
+   closing the menu leaves `BuildMenu` in place with `Visible` off.
+5. Optionally, in Developer Console (F9) > Memory, the `GuiObjects`/Instances count should stay
+   flat while you switch tabs, where before it rose and fell.
